You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Expandable Card (`expandable-card`)

List rows morph into a full dialog: image, title and subtitle fly into place with shared layout animations.

## What it should do
Build expandable cards: a list of rows (thumbnail, title, subtitle) where clicking one opens a centered dialog; the row container, image, title and subtitle each share a `layoutId` (scoped with useId) with the dialog's elements so they morph into place with a spring (260/30). Body content fades in after 150ms. Backdrop blur, Esc to close, focus into dialog and back to the trigger after exit.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion lucide-react`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/expandable-card.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).
- Motion tokens go at `lib/kinetik/tokens.ts` (source below). Use tokens instead of magic numbers.

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** role=dialog + aria-modal, labelled by the title; Esc/backdrop close; focus moves into the dialog and returns to the trigger on close.
- **Performance:** FLIP-based layout animations (transforms only) driven by Motion's layout engine.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

